        Instructions for setting up and running the code
        ================================================

-----------------------------------------------------------------------
@@@          The grid resolution is 1024 x 1024 X 128,             @@@
@@@  f = 1, N = 8 and D = pi/4 so that D/(2*pi) = 128/1024 = 1/8.  @@@
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

To compile all codes needed, go to the src subdirectory (cd src) and type:

make all clean install

Then return to the main directory (cd ..) and set up the initial data with

turb < input_for_turb

then compute the QG balanced flow with

balance

This produces all unscaled fields of interest for Quasi-Geostrophic balance
in the subdirectory qgbal (they can be used as input for PS3D).

#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#-#

There are various (python) plotting scripts.  To plot y = 0 cross sections
of the fields, type

pcross

To plot the surface fields of b, xi, eta and zeta, type

psurf

